        "date": "1845-05-06",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "6 May 1845",
        "text": "In the meantime you do not know what it is to be ... a little afraid of Paracelsus.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s2637",
        "messageOrdinal": 165,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1845-12-04",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "4 December 1845",
        "text": "You will avenge him with the sympathies of the world; that, I foresee....",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s2848",
        "messageOrdinal": 174,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1845-12-16",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "16 December 1845",
        "text": "Now how do you read that omen?",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s4053",
        "messageOrdinal": 221,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-02-05",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "5 February 1846",
        "text": "Unless indeed I should grow painful to you ...",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s6602",
        "messageOrdinal": 331,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1846-04-27",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "27 April 1846",
        "text": "The wind is unremitting,—savage.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s7112",
        "messageOrdinal": 353,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1846-05-12",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "12 May 1846",
        "text": "But goodbye, dearest, till to-morrow—and next day, which is ours.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s7293",
        "messageOrdinal": 363,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1846-05-19",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "19 May 1846",
        "text": "But,—I don’t know why,—I got nervous of a sudden, it seemed late and I remembered the Drawing-room and its occupants.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s9210",
        "messageOrdinal": 446,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-07-08",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "8 July 1846",
        "text": "It will do me good perhaps—but your coming will, certainly.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s10170",
        "messageOrdinal": 484,
        "sender": "Robert",
        "date": "1846-08-03",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "3 August 1846",
        "text": "How you have mistaken my words, whatever they may have been, about the ‘change’ to be expected in my life!",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      },
      {
        "snippetId": "s11300",
        "messageOrdinal": 523,
        "sender": "Elizabeth",
        "date": "1846-08-27",
        "approximate": false,
        "dateLabel": "27 August 1846",
        "text": "I am bound to them utterly.",
        "note": "",
        "callbacks": []
      }
    ]
  }
